Wait for an image to be rendered before presenting it to X11, on kgsl.

Under Xwayland, and in FIFO and immediate mode on any X server, Mesa presents
a swapchain image without waiting for the GPU. It relies on implicit sync:
a DRM driver attaches the rendering fence to the dma-buf, and whoever reads
the buffer waits for it. Qualcomm's kgsl attaches no such fence, and the
kernel interface Mesa would use to attach one itself needs Linux 6.0. On
Android the X server (Termux:X11, or Xwayland under Chameleon) reads the
buffer with the CPU, so it can copy a frame that turnip is still drawing,
which shows as flicker or tearing.

Turnip now tells WSI that it has no implicit sync when it runs on kgsl, and
the X11 present thread then waits for the image's fence before every present,
as it already does in mailbox mode on X servers other than Xwayland. The wait
is in WSI's own thread, not the application's. Other drivers, and turnip on
the msm DRM driver, are unaffected.

--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.h
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.h
@@ -157,6 +157,13 @@
 
    bool sw;
 
+   /* Set by drivers whose kernel driver attaches no fence to a shared buffer
+    * (e.g. Qualcomm's kgsl). A window system that reads a presented image
+    * then has nothing to wait on, so WSI waits for the image to be rendered
+    * before it presents it.
+    */
+   bool no_implicit_sync;
+
    /* Set to true if the implementation is ok with linear WSI images. */
    bool wants_linear;
 
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_x11.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_x11.c
@@ -2520,9 +2520,13 @@
 
       VkPresentModeKHR present_mode = chain->images[image_index].present_mode;
 
-      /* Not necessary to block when we have explicit sync */
+      /* Not necessary to block when we have explicit sync. Without implicit
+       * sync either, the server would read an image that is still being
+       * rendered, in any present mode.
+       */
       bool need_fence_wait =
-            x11_needs_wait_for_fences(chain->base.wsi, wsi_conn, present_mode) &&
+            (x11_needs_wait_for_fences(chain->base.wsi, wsi_conn, present_mode) ||
+             chain->base.wsi->no_implicit_sync) &&
             !chain->base.image_info.explicit_sync;
 
       bool need_timing_fence_wait = x11_swapchain_present_timing_is_out_of_order_completion(
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
@@ -1868,6 +1868,9 @@
       vk_physical_device_finish(&device->vk);
       goto fail_free_name;
    }
+
+   /* kgsl attaches no fences to the dma-bufs it renders to */
+   device->wsi_device.no_implicit_sync = is_kgsl(instance);
 #endif
 
